{"name":"Camping Grounds","hex":"#b4c2a2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"camping grounds","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of camping ground"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/camping_grounds"}],"entries":[{"title":"Campsite","blocks":[{"text":"Campsite, campground, and camping pitch are all related terms regarding a place used for camping. The usage differs between British English and American English."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Camping_Tents_in_the_Woods.jpg/330px-Camping_Tents_in_the_Woods.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Campsite"},{"title":"Camping","blocks":[{"text":"Camping is a form of outdoor recreation or outdoor education involving overnight stays with a basic temporary shelter such as a tent. Camping can also include a recreational vehicle, sheltered cabins, a permanent tent, a shelter such as a bivy or tarp, hammock, or no shelter at all. Typically, participants leave developed areas to spend time outdoors, in pursuit of activities providing them enjoyment or in a form of educational experience. Spending the night away from home distinguishes camping from day-tripping, picnicking, and other outdoor activities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Tent_camping_along_the_Sulayr_trail_in_La_Taha%2C_Sierra_Nevada_National_Park_%28DSCF5147%29.jpg/330px-Tent_camping_along_the_Sulayr_trail_in_La_Taha%2C_Sierra_Nevada_National_Park_%28DSCF5147%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camping"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Ocean_Lakes_Family_Campground.jpg/500px-Ocean_Lakes_Family_Campground.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Ocean_Lake